Id: init013e
Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: tiger tigris
Fix: chown the directory to root (or run from your own checkout with sudo) and chmod go-w it.
References: tigris(8)

The directory Tigris was told to run from (TIGERHOMEDIR, -B, or where
tigris itself is) belongs to someone other than root, the user running
Tigris or the user who invoked sudo, or its group or others may write
it. Everything in it (config, initdefs, every check) is run as whoever
runs Tigris, root as a rule, before any other safeguard: so nothing is
run from a directory someone else could have changed. A clone made
under umask 002, Ubuntu's default for users, is group-writable
throughout: chmod -R go-w it once.
